{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532587-all-editions-do-you-think-the-wyrm-has-a-good-side","id":1532587,"title":"[All Editions]Do you think the wyrm has a \"Good Side\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-03-14T11:14:25-07:00","id":1532587,"title":"[All Editions]Do you think the wyrm has a \"Good Side\"","content":"time to have a discussion that would get us killed if we were Garou for real <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Do you think the wyrm has a &quot;Good Side&quot;? According to Shattered Dreams, it used to be good or at least Not-Evil in the time of the Dragon Kings<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Wyrm has yet to become the Corruptor; the Destroyer is a natural part of Gaia\u2019s balance. Wyrm spirits\u2019<br /> natures are destructive. They\u2019re not reviled for it, but neitherare they summoned for tasks that don\u2019t require breaking<br /> something. Banes don\u2019t exist in this period\u200b </div> </div> </div>Shattered Dreams - PagES 163-164<br /> <br /> So we know for a fact that the Wyrm wasn't always evil. this leads me to a couple questions.<br /> 1)Can it be healed and returned to its Good state?<br /> 2) Can other members of the Triat become the embodiment of Evil instead?<br /> 3)Since the Triat has existed prior the Universe, and the universe is 13 billions years old. Were the Wyld or Weaver ever the embodiment of Evil before the Wyrm become that embodiment?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T11:32:23-07:00","id":1532588,"title":"","content":"Depends on the faction asking the question, doesn't it? I would say good and evil doesn't really factor into the intended function of any member of the Triat in their uncorrupted state - they perform basic tasks that make reality work. They still do in their current state, but arguably the modus is where things went wrong.<br /> <br /> The Ananasi have (had? dunno about W5) the plan to eventually replace the Weaver with her backup copy Ananasa, and in my games I have expanded on that idea with a faction that is also looking into replacing the other members. Current plan for the Wyrm is to somehow separate it from and replace it with Oblivion. That's just them though. But I kind of like the idea of The Endless being able to die and replaced, the Sandman comics handled that concept well and serve as a blueprint for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T11:33:54-07:00","id":1532589,"title":"","content":"The Triat not being evil is a pretty core part of WtA. Uncaring in the way that Great Old Ones are, but when sane none are actively malicious.<br /> <br /> The Wyrm being 'evil' is a side effect of the Weaver trapping it, which they did due to a mixture of grief and not understanding the importance of the Wyrm's role. The issue is that it isn't clear if 1) the Wyrm can be brought back to sanity if and when healed and 2) if the world can survive the Wyrm's release.<br /> <br /> This isn't unknown amongst the Garou, and a number even consider the Weaver the bigger evil (and probably hate the Glass Walkers).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T11:36:21-07:00","id":1532591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532587-all-editions-do-you-think-the-wyrm-has-a-good-side?p=1532588#post1532588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on the faction asking the question, doesn't it? I would say good and evil doesn't really factor into the intended function of any member of the Triat in their uncorrupted state - they perform basic tasks that make reality work. They still do in their current state, but arguably the modus is where things went wrong.<br /> <br /> The Ananasi have (had? dunno about W5) the plan to eventually replace the Weaver with her backup copy Ananasa, and in my games I have expanded on that idea with a faction that is also looking into replacing the other members. Current plan for the Wyrm is to somehow separate it from and replace it with Oblivion. That's just them though. But I kind of like the idea of The Endless being able to die and replaced, the Sandman comics handled that concept well and serve as a blueprint for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>A very good analysis of the Triat. And yeah,the Triat being replaceable is a good idea|<br /> It's worth noting that in those Storyteller Vault Books, the Savage Age ones. The Triat is ever changing, sometimes one of them is evil,one is neutral and the other is good but sometimes they're all indifferent, and even the Wyld could be the &quot;evil one&quot; at some point.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T11:44:28-07:00","id":1532592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532587-all-editions-do-you-think-the-wyrm-has-a-good-side?p=1532589#post1532589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Triat not being evil is a pretty core part of WtA. Uncaring in the way that Great Old Ones are, but when sane none are actively malicious.<br /> <br /> The Wyrm being 'evil' is a side effect of the Weaver trapping it, which they did due to a mixture of grief and not understanding the importance of the Wyrm's role. The issue is that it isn't clear if 1) the Wyrm can be brought back to sanity if and when healed and 2) if the world can survive the Wyrm's release.<br /> <br /> This isn't unknown amongst the Garou, and a number even consider the Weaver the bigger evil (and probably hate the Glass Walkers).</div> </div> </div> </div>oh,i thought the garou were all firmly in camp that nothing could be done about the wyrm and only Bastet and Roqea saw any good in the wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T12:01:18-07:00","id":1532595,"title":"","content":"The triat was never meant to be good or bad, just forces of nature. As TwoSix said, Weaver getting fed up with the Wyrm destroying its creations and wrapping it up is the source of the Wyrm going mad. It got worse and worse as it was kept in its cocoon.<br /> <br /> And I feel this is such a clever twist in the mythology, for all its servants pretend to be its voice, the Wyrm really isn't interested in anything but getting out. Its three heads are the ways it tries to weaken the web.<br /> <br /> There are Wyrm spirits of VERY old age that aren't mad, but they hide because their younger kin are... well, nuts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T12:08:07-07:00","id":1532596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532587-all-editions-do-you-think-the-wyrm-has-a-good-side?p=1532595#post1532595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The triat was never meant to be good or bad, just forces of nature. As TwoSix said, Weaver getting fed up with the Wyrm destroying its creations and wrapping it up is the source of the Wyrm going mad. It got worse and worse as it was kept in its cocoon.<br /> <br /> And I feel this is such a clever twist in the mythology, for all its servants pretend to be its voice, the Wyrm really isn't interested in anything but getting out. Its three heads are the ways it tries to weaken the web.<br /> <br /> There are Wyrm spirits of VERY old age that aren't mad, but they hide because their younger kin are... well, nuts.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is very clever<br /> I didn't know there were any wyrm spirits left that were'nt banes, what they like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T12:19:01-07:00","id":1532600,"title":"","content":"I think every edition has, to a greater or lesser degree, maintained that the pre-fall aspects of the Wyrm are still largely chugging along although they do also get co-opted or gangpressed to assist the three-heads and the banes from time to time.<br /> <br /> Generally the pre-fall Wyrm spirits are described as being those naturally involved with decay, disintegration, culling, etc. Literal worms are perhaps the archetypal examples alongside other decomposers, and by extension, scavengers in general. Disease is usually also given a Wyrmish character although imo an argument can also be made there for Wyld influence but I don\u2019t think it\u2019s solely one of the other. Examples would range from certain types of mushroom, maggots, flies, vultures, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T12:28:41-07:00","id":1532601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532587-all-editions-do-you-think-the-wyrm-has-a-good-side#post1532587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So we know for a fact that the Wyrm wasn't always evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fact is kind of stretching things a bit. WtA's mythology (and the many take on it from the multitude of factions within it) is based on enough observable things that there are somethings most WtA factions agree on as &quot;history.&quot;<br /> <br /> That said, I'll echo the idea that &quot;good&quot; and &quot;evil&quot; are concepts ill-suited to the Triat. What makes the Triat's current state so dangerous is imbalance and strife taking over the trio.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1)Can it be healed and returned to its Good state? </div> </div> </div>Maybe. It's certainly possible in theory. Whether or not anything is capable of pulling it off is another matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) Can other members of the Triat become the embodiment of Evil instead? </div> </div> </div>As noted, plenty of groups in WtA already think the Weaver is just as bad if not worse than the Wyrm. Again, avoiding the labeling side of things, it's painfully easy to shift the Weaver into the primary antagonist patron over the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> The Wyld is difficult because the Wyld, unlike the Weaver and Wyrm, is incapable of having any long term agenda. The Wyld ascending to being the most dangerous of the Triat would mean a world where the very fundamental laws of nature are constantly in flux. The &quot;best case&quot; scenario for this as a playable setting would end up looking kind of like Creation in Exalted, where there's an island of stable reality held together by all of the most powerful Gaia and Helios aligned spirits, surrounded by an endless Flux Realm beyond constantly trying to eat at the edges of normal existence. It's possible metaphysically, but you'd have a vastly different game on your hands.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3)Since the Triat has existed prior the Universe, and the universe is 13 billions years old. Were the Wyld or Weaver ever the embodiment of Evil before the Wyrm become that embodiment? </div> </div> </div>There's a ton of assumptions in this question that don't follow the facts in evidence and thus this really can't be answered effectively beyond the previous points about how poorly labelling the Triat like this goes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T12:33:50-07:00","id":1532602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532587-all-editions-do-you-think-the-wyrm-has-a-good-side?p=1532601#post1532601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fact is kind of stretching things a bit. WtA's mythology (and the many take on it from the multitude of factions within it) is based on enough observable things that there are somethings most WtA factions agree on as &quot;history.&quot;<br /> <br /> That said, I'll echo the idea that &quot;good&quot; and &quot;evil&quot; are concepts ill-suited to the Triat. What makes the Triat's current state so dangerous is imbalance and strife taking over the trio.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Maybe. It's certainly possible in theory. Whether or not anything is capable of pulling it off is another matter.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As noted, plenty of groups in WtA already think the Weaver is just as bad if not worse than the Wyrm. Again, avoiding the labeling side of things, it's painfully easy to shift the Weaver into the primary antagonist patron over the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> The Wyld is difficult because the Wyld, unlike the Weaver and Wyrm, is incapable of having any long term agenda. The Wyld ascending to being the most dangerous of the Triat would mean a world where the very fundamental laws of nature are constantly in flux. The &quot;best case&quot; scenario for this as a playable setting would end up looking kind of like Creation in Exalted, where there's an island of stable reality held together by all of the most powerful Gaia and Helios aligned spirits, surrounded by an endless Flux Realm beyond constantly trying to eat at the edges of normal existence. It's possible metaphysically, but you'd have a vastly different game on your hands.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> There's a ton of assumptions in this question that don't follow the facts in evidence and thus this really can't be answered effectively beyond the previous points about how poorly labelling the Triat like this goes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks Heavy, the Wyld acting as it's namesake on Exakted didn't occur to me","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T12:34:59-07:00","id":1532603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532587-all-editions-do-you-think-the-wyrm-has-a-good-side?p=1532600#post1532600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think every edition has, to a greater or lesser degree, maintained that the pre-fall aspects of the Wyrm are still largely chugging along although they do also get co-opted or gangpressed to assist the three-heads and the banes from time to time.<br /> <br /> Generally the pre-fall Wyrm spirits are described as being those naturally involved with decay, disintegration, culling, etc. Literal worms are perhaps the archetypal examples alongside other decomposers, and by extension, scavengers in general. Disease is usually also given a Wyrmish character although imo an argument can also be made there for Wyld influence but I don\u2019t think it\u2019s solely one of the other. Examples would range from certain types of mushroom, maggots, flies, vultures, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh so basically they were kin to animals who are very creepy yet indescribably necessary to the ecosystem to work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T13:42:40-07:00","id":1532606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532587-all-editions-do-you-think-the-wyrm-has-a-good-side#post1532587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So we know for a fact that the Wyrm wasn't always evil. this leads me to a couple questions.<br /> 1)Can it be healed and returned to its Good state?</div> </div> </div> </div>The scenario Weaver Ascendant from Apocalypse certainly seems to think that there's a shot at it, if a slim one without a lot of things going the way of the folks who want to make it work. It even has a rite for making it happen and a rundown of what succeeding might mean (while no disease would be worse, the cure has some pretty significant ramifications for the cosmos as a whole).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) Can other members of the Triat become the embodiment of Evil instead? </div> </div> </div>Again, Weaver Ascendant. The fact that it's in Apocalypse, the capstone of the line before W20, should speak volumes about that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3)Since the Triat has existed prior the Universe, and the universe is 13 billions years old. Were the Wyld or Weaver ever the embodiment of Evil before the Wyrm become that embodiment? </div> </div> </div>Book of the Wyld discusses what a world with a Wyld that's twisted and causing trouble would look like. It was technically written with Revised in mind (it uses Essence instead of Power for spirits), so it might also be worth looking into if you want to explore the concept. Exalted is also a possibility - the Wyld in it is a roiling ocean of chaos around an island of stability where identity and solidity are possible. The first two editions also gave the mutations that it induced very negative names - poxes, afflictions, blights, and abominations, in order of least to highest in terms of significance, even though they usually had some very useful effects. The negative mutations also shared the name of the &quot;counterbalancing&quot; traits of Possessed, Taints.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T15:50:34-07:00","id":1532618,"title":"","content":"I hold that the Triat is just Garou mythology that anthropomorphizes the metaphysic trinity of Mage. Dynamism becomes the Wyld. Stasis becomes the Weaver. Entropy becomes the Wyrm. It's just the physics of the World of Darkness. It's akin to making up gods based on gravity, electromagnetism, the strong force, and the weak force. They're neither good or evil. But in addition to &quot;Wyrm&quot; being Entropy (the Balance Wyrm), &quot;Wyrm&quot; is also used to denote the force of supernatural evil in the world. Call it Satan, Melkor/Morgoth, Leviathan, Nidhoggr, Ahriman, Typhon, Apep, Wyrm, Oblivion, or whatever. <br /> <br /> The Garou just join the two and then come up with a reason why things &quot;changed&quot;. It's their answer to the philosophical Problem of Evil. It's also why they further subdivided the Wyrm into the Beast of War, Eater of Souls, and the Defiler Wyrm.<br /> <br /> The Garou are very knowledgeable, but also have their own biases, ignorance, and superstition. I don't believe in silo-ing the original games of the World of Darkness. They were clearly intended to work together and be linked. So this is how I do it. Others may do it a different way, or just prefer each game does its own thing and has all the answers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T16:07:54-07:00","id":1532619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532587-all-editions-do-you-think-the-wyrm-has-a-good-side?p=1532618#post1532618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hold that the Triat is just Garou mythology that anthropomorphizes the metaphysic trinity of Mage. Dynamism becomes the Wyld. Stasis becomes the Weaver. Entropy becomes the Wyrm. It's just the physics of the World of Darkness. It's akin to making up gods based on gravity, electromagnetism, the strong force, and the weak force. They're neither good or evil. But in addition to &quot;Wyrm&quot; being Entropy (the Balance Wyrm), &quot;Wyrm&quot; is also used to denote the force of supernatural evil in the world. Call it Satan, Melkor/Morgoth, Leviathan, Nidhoggr, Ahriman, Typhon, Apep, Wyrm, Oblivion, or whatever.<br /> <br /> The Garou just join the two and then come up with a reason why things &quot;changed&quot;. It's their answer to the philosophical Problem of Evil. It's also why they further subdivided the Wyrm into the Beast of War, Eater of Souls, and the Defiler Wyrm.<br /> <br /> The Garou are very knowledgeable, but also have their own biases, ignorance, and superstition. I don't believe in silo-ing the original games of the World of Darkness. They were clearly intended to work together and be linked. So this is how I do it. Others may do it a different way, or just prefer each game does its own thing and has all the answers.</div> </div> </div> </div>cool stuff,even if it's not necessarily how i'd run it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T16:12:58-07:00","id":1532620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532587-all-editions-do-you-think-the-wyrm-has-a-good-side?p=1532618#post1532618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hold that the Triat is just Garou mythology that anthropomorphizes the metaphysic trinity of Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not even going to post the link to the Abridged Cell quote. I'm just going to say you do you, but that's very far away from the books, since the Triat are still incomprehensibly huge and not really approachable according to the Garou. So there's not really much in the way of human qualities ascribed to them, at least if you're a Theurge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dynamism becomes the Wyld. Stasis becomes the Weaver. Entropy becomes the Wyrm. It's just the physics of the World of Darkness. It's akin to making up gods based on gravity, electromagnetism, the strong force, and the weak force. They're neither good or evil. But in addition to &quot;Wyrm&quot; being Entropy (the Balance Wyrm), &quot;Wyrm&quot; is also used to denote the force of supernatural evil in the world. Call it Satan, Melkor/Morgoth, Leviathan, Nidhoggr, Ahriman, Typhon, Apep, Wyrm, Oblivion, or whatever.<br /> <br /> The Garou just join the two and then come up with a reason why things &quot;changed&quot;. It's their answer to the philosophical Problem of Evil. It's also why they further subdivided the Wyrm into the Beast of War, Eater of Souls, and the Defiler Wyrm.<br /> <br /> The Garou are very knowledgeable, but also have their own biases, ignorance, and superstition. I don't believe in silo-ing the original games of the World of Darkness. They were clearly intended to work together and be linked. So this is how I do it. Others may do it a different way, or just prefer each game does its own thing and has all the answers. </div> </div> </div>No, they weren't. In fact, at some point, they became intentionally incompatible with each other in any function but via basic rules, and sometimes not even then. The rift starts at Leadership being a Talent instead of a skill and magnifies until Werewolf Deep Umbra is a world of abstractions behind a second Gauntlet comparable to the High Umbra and Mage Deep Umbra is space. 20th anniversary editions changed that again, but Mage still treats most of space as the Umbra, which Werewolf does not. Vampire wants you to put murder of other humans as the deepest sin; other games aren't really as certain. Mage posits that humans are the most important things in the universe; Werewolf <i>violently</i> disagrees at putting humans on a pedestal.<br /> <br /> Each game has a very different set of priorities, message, style of play, and intended threats. Trying to muscle into Werewolf territory in particular tends to end up with a lot of misgivings over characters from most other games being torn apart like tissue paper in a random fight with a relatively unremarkable combat fomor.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T16:49:14-07:00","id":1532624,"title":"","content":"Werewolf is a game with animism deep in it's core. You can go talk to a spirit of gravity that exists independent of the Garou. The idea that the Triat is some sort of sole exception where there are no spirits of something fundamental feels like sacrificing far too much of WtA's themes to force it to bow to Mage for compatibility... despite the fact that Mage never discounts the idea that the Triat exists as spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-15T02:16:16-07:00","id":1532639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532587-all-editions-do-you-think-the-wyrm-has-a-good-side?p=1532596#post1532596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is very clever<br /> I didn't know there were any wyrm spirits left that were'nt banes, what they like?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Elder_Serpent\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Elder_Serpent</a><br /> <br /> Older Brothers Patron is said by some Garou to be a servant of the Balance Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-15T05:52:14-07:00","id":1532646,"title":"","content":"That's very cool","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-15T12:19:51-07:00","id":1532661,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve said it before and will say it again - a lot of WEREWOLF 5th Edition\u2019s basic assumptions make so much more sense of you assume that the Weaver is the Big Bad in that version of the setting.<br /> <br /> The difficulties piercing the veil, the emphasis on trying new &amp; different approaches to being a Werewolf, Cockroach being kicked to the curb by the Glass Walkers in favour of Spider (I\u2019m not saying Roach spirits HAVE to be all passive aggressive to the Walkers, but it\u2019s a perfectly valid excuse for a running joke), the running theme that Evil is more like gravity than a wildlife \u2026 <br /> <br /> <br /> A thallus, I really like the idea of there being a cycle over the course of which the various members of the Triat wax &amp; wane in terms of Power &amp; Dangerousness (With EXALTED showing what happens when the Wyld gets a bit too potent).<br /> <br /> <br /> I\u2019m a little torn over <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>\u2019s suggested cosmology - it\u2019s a perfectly plausible, indeed intriguing, vision of things that I can imagine using: on the other hand I\u2019m a bit of a purist at heart and enjoy trying to work out what the best balance between the individual Game line\u2019s cosmology and the sense of a World of Darkness greater than a single line might be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-15T20:48:23-07:00","id":1532679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532587-all-editions-do-you-think-the-wyrm-has-a-good-side?p=1532618#post1532618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hold that the Triat is just Garou mythology that anthropomorphizes the metaphysic trinity of Mage. Dynamism becomes the Wyld. Stasis becomes the Weaver. Entropy becomes the Wyrm. It's just the physics of the World of Darkness. It's akin to making up gods based on gravity, electromagnetism, the strong force, and the weak force. They're neither good or evil. But in addition to &quot;Wyrm&quot; being Entropy (the Balance Wyrm), &quot;Wyrm&quot; is also used to denote the force of supernatural evil in the world. Call it Satan, Melkor/Morgoth, Leviathan, Nidhoggr, Ahriman, Typhon, Apep, Wyrm, Oblivion, or whatever.<br /> <br /> The Garou just join the two and then come up with a reason why things &quot;changed&quot;. It's their answer to the philosophical Problem of Evil. It's also why they further subdivided the Wyrm into the Beast of War, Eater of Souls, and the Defiler Wyrm.<br /> <br /> The Garou are very knowledgeable, but also have their own biases, ignorance, and superstition. I don't believe in silo-ing the original games of the World of Darkness. They were clearly intended to work together and be linked. So this is how I do it. Others may do it a different way, or just prefer each game does its own thing and has all the answers.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is an interesting idea, though of course it runs into issues that the Wyrm has magical servants who worship and follow it and also most of them make the same sort of claims that Garou do. And many non-Garou also acknowledge the Wyrm-as-corrupted (like the werespiders), so it's definitely not just a Garou thing. Plus with the ability to &quot;Sense Wyrm&quot; in older editions, it would ping on both corrupted and older non-corrupted Wyrm entities. So it's seems fairly certain that in Werewolf, at some point the metaphysical concept of entropy was thrown off kilter somehow and is now fundamentally broken. <br /> <br /> Of course, you tie that back to Mage if you want. I recall various theories from Mage fans that Entropy/Necromancy has been fundamentally broken and twisted (possibly by Voormas or other Barrabi), such that any powerful Necromancer inevitably seeks to tear down the wall between the living and the dead. If we go with the idea that Entropy (the Wyrm) itself was twisted or corrupted at some point, you can use that as a basic concept within both Mage and Werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T20:21:59-07:00","id":1532748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532587-all-editions-do-you-think-the-wyrm-has-a-good-side?p=1532679#post1532679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is an interesting idea, though of course it runs into issues that the Wyrm has magical servants who worship and follow it and also most of them make the same sort of claims that Garou do. And many non-Garou also acknowledge the Wyrm-as-corrupted (like the werespiders), so it's definitely not just a Garou thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, there is a certainly a &quot;Malfean cosmology&quot; out there. We see it in the Nephandi too. And it appears in human various occult texts mentioned in the game (both Werewolf and Mage). All that means it is an independent occult tradition, likely arising out of Changing Breed mythology/religion that bled over to humanity through their kinfolk. But that doesn't mean it isn't any more &quot;true&quot; than all the other Nephandi or occultists who worship Satan, Ahriman, or Nyarlathotep. Rather than saying one is objectively true or the others are objectively wrong, I like to treat it that everybody is just looking through a glass darkly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532587-all-editions-do-you-think-the-wyrm-has-a-good-side?p=1532679#post1532679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus with the ability to &quot;Sense Wyrm&quot; in older editions, it would ping on both corrupted and older non-corrupted Wyrm entities.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Gift Sense Wyrm obviously detects something objectively. But many STs struggle how to depict it without it becoming a &quot;Detect Evil&quot; spell. There's lot of interpretations. The one I use in my chronicles is that it acts like a Geiger counter. It detects some form of spiritual pollution that is anathema/harmful/alien to Gaia. But it is not infallible, and it doesn't always mean what people may initially think it means. Lots of Wyrm creatures don't detect as the Wyrm. Things like ghosts aren't necessarily evil, but they are also not part of the Gaian cycle, and when their presence affects the Skinlands it detects as Wyrm. And I hold that things like a miner getting black lung or someone dying of cancer also detects as &quot;Wyrm&quot;. Not to mention mundane things like industrial pollution. I think Sense Wyrm should be used as the starting point of the PCs investigating something, not a reason to kill everything they find. And of course one reason PENTEX and others like to spread around Wyrm tainted products is that it pretty much makes everything detect as Wyrm, rendering it useless.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532587-all-editions-do-you-think-the-wyrm-has-a-good-side?p=1532679#post1532679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it's seems fairly certain that in Werewolf, at some point the metaphysical concept of entropy was thrown off kilter somehow and is now fundamentally broken.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is just another restatement of the Problem of Evil. Why do bad things happen to good people? Why is their death, misery, and suffering in the world? Philosophers and theologians have debated this for thousands of years. Why was paradise lost? Is it because Pandora opened the box? Is it because Eve ate the apple? Is it because the world is an illusion? Is it because the Mandate of Heaven has been lost? Is it that Evil actually rules the world and good is wrong? Is it because Melkor created discord in the music of creation? Is it because the Weaver trapped the Wyrm? It's just that in the World of Darkness, supernatural forces are an outright fact and are a part of the equation. So besides the natural evils we experience in the real world, we also have active supernatural forces and creatures inflicting evil on the world.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T22:33:29-07:00","id":1532756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532587-all-editions-do-you-think-the-wyrm-has-a-good-side?p=1532748#post1532748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep, there is a certainly a &quot;Malfean cosmology&quot; out there. We see it in the Nephandi too. And it appears in human various occult texts mentioned in the game (both Werewolf and Mage). All that means it is an independent occult tradition, likely arising out of Changing Breed mythology/religion that bled over to humanity through their kinfolk. But that doesn't mean it isn't any more &quot;true&quot; than all the other Nephandi or occultists who worship Satan, Ahriman, or Nyarlathotep. Rather than saying one is objectively true or the others are objectively wrong, I like to treat it that everybody is just looking through a glass darkly.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're told most of what we know about W:tA's cosmology out of character, with no unrealiable narrators. In fact, the text calls out when the narrators are unrealiable, and when they are closer to what the text knows.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Gift Sense Wyrm obviously detects something objectively. But many STs struggle how to depict it without it becoming a &quot;Detect Evil&quot; spell. </div> </div> </div>Except that we have a lot of text boxes to show the difference. And points in rather aged essays (Ethan Skemp had a lot of words to say about this important points of the game in the 2nd edition player's guide) about how picking up on the feeling of it is a bit incidental.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's lot of interpretations. </div> </div> </div>Not really. It's been fairly well covered by now, which is why the mischaracterization of it in the W5 dev diaries is so galling. So there isn't a feeling of spiritual defilement that follows vampires around? Well, to be frank, I wouldn't have bothered to check if I were confronted with a stable of addicted slaves, persistent influence of a vampire in making sure that neighborhoods are shit, and possibly also <i>a literal flesh cave</i>. Those are so blatant that the stench in legacy would have been overpowering, and it would have stuck to the victims and attracted more banes, unfortunately, until a rite of purification happened.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The one I use in my chronicles is that it acts like a Geiger counter. It detects some form of spiritual pollution that is anathema/harmful/alien to Gaia. But it is not infallible, and it doesn't always mean what people may initially think it means. Lots of Wyrm creatures don't detect as the Wyrm. </div> </div> </div>Canonically, even the Elder Serpent, a relic of an uncorrupted Wyrm, still registers rather strongly on Sense Wyrm, as would similarly uncorrupted fragments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Things like ghosts aren't necessarily evil, but they are also not part of the Gaian cycle, and when their presence affects the Skinlands it detects as Wyrm. </div> </div> </div>By RAW not unless the ghost's Angst is higher than its Willpower or it is outright a specter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I hold that things like a miner getting black lung or someone dying of cancer also detects as &quot;Wyrm&quot;. Not to mention mundane things like industrial pollution. I think Sense Wyrm should be used as the starting point of the PCs investigating something, not a reason to kill everything they find. And of course one reason PENTEX and others like to spread around Wyrm tainted products is that it pretty much makes everything detect as Wyrm, rendering it useless. </div> </div> </div>But it's also a special thing, which usually indicates that there's been bane activity. Hence, the line in the 2nd edition player's guide essay about how it doesn't mean that devil made you do it - you did it, and the devil noticed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is just another restatement of the Problem of Evil. </div> </div> </div>Not as long as you don't feel that God has to exist in the WoD. No omnipotent being, no problem of evil! While Garou and Fera have certainly claimed a lot of things about powerful spirits, omnipotence, omniscience and what have you have not been among them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why do bad things happen to good people? Why is their death, misery, and suffering in the world? Philosophers and theologians have debated this for thousands of years. Why was paradise lost? Is it because Pandora opened the box? Is it because Eve ate the apple? Is it because the world is an illusion? Is it because the Mandate of Heaven has been lost? Is it that Evil actually rules the world and good is wrong? Is it because Melkor created discord in the music of creation? Is it because the Weaver trapped the Wyrm? It's just that in the World of Darkness, supernatural forces are an outright fact and are a part of the equation. So besides the natural evils we experience in the real world, we also have active supernatural forces and creatures inflicting evil on the world. </div> </div> </div>Again, as long as you don't posit that there's some all-powerful force that could prevent everything bad but doesn't, is there really a Problem of Evil? The state is far more like how Setsuna in Gundam OO characterizes the state of the world - twisted, and he frequently comes face to face with the ones responsible for twisting it, so it's not really much of a philosophical mystery so much as it was a naked power grab by control freaks with no capacity for trust.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-21T13:21:57-07:00","id":1532958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532587-all-editions-do-you-think-the-wyrm-has-a-good-side#post1532587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">time to have a discussion that would get us killed if we were Garou for real <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Do you think the wyrm has a &quot;Good Side&quot;? According to Shattered Dreams, it used to be good or at least Not-Evil in the time of the Dragon Kings<br /> <br /> <br /> Shattered Dreams - PagES 163-164<br /> <br /> So we know for a fact that the Wyrm wasn't always evil. this leads me to a couple questions.<br /> 1)Can it be healed and returned to its Good state?<br /> 2) Can other members of the Triat become the embodiment of Evil instead?<br /> 3)Since the Triat has existed prior the Universe, and the universe is 13 billions years old. Were the Wyld or Weaver ever the embodiment of Evil before the Wyrm become that embodiment?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) In older editions the Wyrm could potentially be healed. Especially since killing it would lead to a complete destruction of a fundamental force in the Universe. In the Weaver Unleased scenario in the Apocalypse Time of Judgement book we see the Weaver as the primary antagonist and healing the Wyrm as the ultimate goal of that scenario.<br /> <br /> 2) The Weaver is sometimes posted a the true antagonist of the game. Especially in Revised books. There is also a &quot;What If&quot; alternate timeline idea in the Storyteller's Handbook Revised where the Wyld is out of control and keeps turning out new life over crowding the earth. The Wyrm and Weaver are struggling to keep up and if the Wyld succeeds all existence will be a chaotic storm where nothing truly exists for very long.<br /> <br /> 3) Unclear. There were some hints that Exalted was a prequel to WoD (this was later dropped) and the Wyld was certainly more of an antagonist than what would become the Weaver. Before the universe it was likely that there was only Wyrm (balance and nothingness) or Wyle (pure possibility). But that's only speculation on my part","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28181-a-bunch-of-gamers","name":"A Bunch of Gamers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28181_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-21T14:48:08-07:00","id":1532963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A Bunch of Gamers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532587-all-editions-do-you-think-the-wyrm-has-a-good-side?p=1532958#post1532958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) Unclear. There were some hints that Exalted was a prequel to WoD (this was later dropped) and the Wyld was certainly more of an antagonist than what would become the Weaver. Before the universe it was likely that there was only Wyrm (balance and nothingness) or Wyle (pure possibility). But that's only speculation on my part</div> </div> </div> </div>That was the Mokole's understanding in their old breed book.<br /> Their take is: The Unmaker was first, sleeping in the depths of a dark nothingness(possibly dead previous verse), and the Wyld burst out of nowhere like the fucking Coolade Man. The resulting fight between the newborn wYld and a Very confused Unmaker led to so much disorganized chaos from constant making/unmaking that the Weaver was born(Likely the shear force of it's own OCD-compelled need to organize it all).<br /> They tend to agree with the ananasi on the idea that gaia came After the triat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-21T15:52:03-07:00","id":1532965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532587-all-editions-do-you-think-the-wyrm-has-a-good-side?p=1532963#post1532963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was the Mokole's understanding in their old breed book.<br /> Their take is: The Unmaker was first, sleeping in the depths of a dark nothingness(possibly dead previous verse), and the Wyld burst out of nowhere like the fucking Coolade Man. The resulting fight between the newborn wYld and a Very confused Unmaker led to so much disorganized chaos from constant making/unmaking that the Weaver was born(Likely the shear force of it's own OCD-compelled need to organize it all).<br /> They tend to agree with the ananasi on the idea that gaia came After the triat.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Mokole don't purport to actually know that, in the breed book or out, because as they get tired of emphasizing, they weren't here to see the creation of everything, damnit. They're not nearly that old. No form of life was.<br /> <br /> (I re-read the book just now and that reference doesn't seem to exist in the narrative framing of Peter Ward getting his crash course in being Mokole. Nor in the Book of the Wyld with Ladon. Are you sure you have the right book?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-21T16:39:11-07:00","id":1532971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532587-all-editions-do-you-think-the-wyrm-has-a-good-side?p=1532965#post1532965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I re-read the book just now and that reference doesn't seem to exist in the narrative framing of Peter Ward getting his crash course in being Mokole. Nor in the Book of the Wyld with Ladon. Are you sure you have the right book?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Nevermind, I got the breed-book 6(Mokole) and 7(Ananasi) mixed up. The Spiders seem to be the only ones who have the opinion that the Uncreator was the first to exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-24T10:00:27-07:00","id":1533079,"title":"","content":"Okay, I'm a little late in this conversation, but here's my two cents. I believe so, the Wyrm could be good, after all the triad seems to have a function that at least in theory would work, after all the Wyrm should devour life so that it doesn't become overwhelmed, besides I believe that the Weaver and the Wyld itself They could also get out of control and would try to take advantage if given the opportunity.<br /> <br /> In Weaver's case I believe there wouldn't be much mystery, it seems very methodical, cold and bound by order, so if it were in control would try one of two options. The first would be to control all life and make the animals, plants and humans follow their functions in the food chain without much differentiation, new species wouldn't be created unnecessarily and there would be strict population control in order to facilitate the administration, human beings would have lives focused on work and the proliferation of the species and the jobs would be decided by their ability alone, and anyone who deviated from the norm would be erased, whether due to opinion or physical/psychological problem, they live basically like drones in this scenario. The second scenario would be a world devoid of animal or plant life, only occupied by non-living mineral beings, a still and static world, therefore ordered and organized.<br /> <br /> In the case of the Wyld, it isn't necessary to think much, it wants to continue creating things and without something to stop it, that is what it would continue to do, probably creating new living beings that could only be described as aberrations and even monuments made entirely of plants or meat, like mountains made of muscles for example. Another way to think about what the end result would be, there was a Marvel comic in which the heroes discovered a universe where death didn't exist and the entire universe just continued to expand like a huge cancer without dying and in perpetual suffering, I think it would be something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-28T13:54:06-07:00","id":1533329,"title":"","content":"I play with a not evil Wyrm. Cancer isn't evil, radiation isn't evil. Gaia wants to still alive, and that is why the Garou see it as evil, it was all a Gaia lie","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28021-camaradadoppio","name":"CamaradaDoppio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28021_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-28T16:22:58-07:00","id":1533334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CamaradaDoppio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532587-all-editions-do-you-think-the-wyrm-has-a-good-side?p=1533329#post1533329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I play with a not evil Wyrm. Cancer isn't evil, radiation isn't evil. Gaia wants to still alive, and that is why the Garou see it as evil, it was all a Gaia lie</div> </div> </div> </div>There might not be any moral judgments inherent in them but they're still dangerous, and long-term, cancer wouldn't be able to survive outside of an environment in solution with infinite amount of nutrients, as it just doesn't stop growing. A curious pairing in your post, too, as the latter tends to kill the former more readily, along with other fast-dividing cells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-05T08:06:25-07:00","id":1533612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532587-all-editions-do-you-think-the-wyrm-has-a-good-side?p=1533334#post1533334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There might not be any moral judgments inherent in them but they're still dangerous, and long-term, cancer wouldn't be able to survive outside of an environment in solution with infinite amount of nutrients, as it just doesn't stop growing. A curious pairing in your post, too, as the latter tends to kill the former more readily, along with other fast-dividing cells.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cancer and Radiation are the most common things in Wyrm imaginery. Yes, they are dangerous, but they are not EVIL. And that's my point","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28021-camaradadoppio","name":"CamaradaDoppio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28021_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-26T14:38:39-07:00","id":1534780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532587-all-editions-do-you-think-the-wyrm-has-a-good-side?p=1532679#post1532679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is an interesting idea, though of course it runs into issues that the Wyrm has magical servants who worship and follow it and also most of them make the same sort of claims that Garou do. And many non-Garou also acknowledge the Wyrm-as-corrupted (like the werespiders), so it's definitely not just a Garou thing. Plus with the ability to &quot;Sense Wyrm&quot; in older editions, it would ping on both corrupted and older non-corrupted Wyrm entities. So it's seems fairly certain that in Werewolf, at some point the metaphysical concept of entropy was thrown off kilter somehow and is now fundamentally broken.<br /> <br /> Of course, you tie that back to Mage if you want. I recall various theories from Mage fans that Entropy/Necromancy has been fundamentally broken and twisted (possibly by Voormas or other Barrabi), such that any powerful Necromancer inevitably seeks to tear down the wall between the living and the dead. If we go with the idea that Entropy (the Wyrm) itself was twisted or corrupted at some point, you can use that as a basic concept within both Mage and Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have even today nutjobs that claim they do it for God while we do not even know if God want this. So I could very easy imagine some Spirits rever the wyrms destructive potential and because they want it they start to think that the Wyrm want it too while actual the Wyrm just want out of this <i>*censored*</i> net.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532587-all-editions-do-you-think-the-wyrm-has-a-good-side?p=1532748#post1532748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The Gift Sense Wyrm obviously detects something objectively. But many STs struggle how to depict it without it becoming a &quot;Detect Evil&quot; spell. There's lot of interpretations. The one I use in my chronicles is that it acts like a Geiger counter. It detects some form of spiritual pollution that is anathema/harmful/alien to Gaia. But it is not infallible, and it doesn't always mean what people may initially think it means. Lots of Wyrm creatures don't detect as the Wyrm. Things like ghosts aren't necessarily evil, but they are also not part of the Gaian cycle, and when their presence affects the Skinlands it detects as Wyrm. And I hold that things like a miner getting black lung or someone dying of cancer also detects as &quot;Wyrm&quot;. Not to mention mundane things like industrial pollution. I think Sense Wyrm should be used as the starting point of the PCs investigating something, not a reason to kill everything they find. And of course one reason PENTEX and others like to spread around Wyrm tainted products is that it pretty much makes everything detect as Wyrm, rendering it useless.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is even part of WtA why Pentex is so problematic. Many of their inventions heal and support humans only to poisen them with wyrm taint in the long run. So Garou only see a lot of corrupted people that are all the victims and have trouble with this ability to discern the TRULY corrupted.<br /> <br /> But back to topic yeah I think the wyrm has a good side as the wyrm cut of harmful things and in the end make sure there is no overgrowth. Sure first eternal growth may look good. But everything is laugh and joy until someone gets cancer. And just like cancer may be still healt with chemo and radiation so is the wyrm, well if he would not be entangeld by the weaver.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}